; A clock-in/clock-out line may end right after its time
; ("o 2024/01/15 17:00:00", 21 characters).  Such a line names no
; account, payee or note.  The parser reuses one line buffer, so the
; bytes past the line's end belong to an earlier, longer line and
; must never be read as this line's account, payee or note.

; (a) A long comment between the check-in and a bare check-out.
i 2024/01/15 09:00:00 Alpha
; xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx Beta  stale note
o 2024/01/15 17:00:00

; (b) A check-out line whose trailing space the reader strips.
i 2024/01/16 09:00:00 Gamma
o 2024/01/16 17:00:00 

; (c) The check-in carries a payee and a note, which the entry keeps.
i 2024/01/17 09:00:00 Delta  Client call  ; billable
o 2024/01/17 12:30:00

; (d) A bare capital-O check-out after a long comment clears the entry.
i 2024/01/19 09:00:00 Zeta
; xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx Eta  another stale note
O 2024/01/19 10:00:00

test reg
24-Jan-15                       Alpha                         8.00h        8.00h
24-Jan-16                       Gamma                         8.00h       16.00h
24-Jan-17 Client call           Delta                         3.50h       19.50h
24-Jan-19                       Zeta                          1.00h       20.50h
end test

test reg --format "%(date)|%(code)|%(payee)|%(account)|%(note)|%(amount)\n"
2024/01/15|||Alpha||28800s
2024/01/16|||Gamma||28800s
2024/01/17||Client call|Delta|billable|12600s
2024/01/19|||Zeta||3600s
end test

test reg --cleared
24-Jan-19                       Zeta                          1.00h        1.00h
end test
